  "basis": "HOURLY, NOT ANNUAL. h_p50 = median hourly earnings from wages and salaries, gross (before tax), for wage and salary earners, by occupation, from the income supplement of Stats NZ's Household Labour Force Survey, June 2019 quarter, exactly as published (NZD per hour). Stats NZ published only the median for this breakdown on www.stats.govt.nz, so h_p10/h_p25/h_p75/h_p90/h_mean are null. No hourly-to-annual conversion has been applied: the source gives no hours worked by occupation, so every annual field (p10..p90, mean) is null. employees is null because the number of wage and salary earners per occupation is not published on www.stats.govt.nz; employed_total is a different measure: all people employed in that occupation group (employees plus employers and self-employed), HLFS quarterly series, June 2019 quarter, both sexes, published in thousands and multiplied by 1,000. all_occupations is a national benchmark, not an occupation figure: median weekly earnings from wages and salaries for all wage and salary earners (w_p50, as published), with p50 = w_p50 x 52.",
